atem:
  line: The Hollins Lane orchard produced 140 litres of juice this year, up from 90 last year, and the group agreed
    to ask the council to wait until September to mow the meadow strip to protect pollinators.
  focus: The text details the orchard's increased juice yield and the group's plan to delay mowing. The author highlights
    the dependency between the meadow strip and fruit pollination.
  push: The reader should support the request to delay mowing to protect the pollinators essential for the orchard's
    fruit production.
  pull: The text assumes the meadow strip is the primary pollinator source and that the council will accept the
    delay request.
